        <title type="html"><![CDATA[Update SuppressedError specification links to ECMA-262]]></title>
        <id>https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/30784</id>
        <link href="https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/30784"/>
        <updated>2026-10-07T17:50:18.000Z</updated>
        <content type="html"><![CDATA[<img src="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/12343178?u=5709fea5745a389a2ce2bf522e57aef637a62ba1&v=4" width="64" height="64" alt=""/><br/><h4 dir="auto">Summary</h4>
<p dir="auto">Update the specification links for <code class="notranslate">SuppressedError</code>, its constructor, and its <code class="notranslate">error</code> and <code class="notranslate">suppressed</code> properties to ECMA-262.</p>
<p dir="auto">The <a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/JavaScript/Reference/Global_Objects/SuppressedError/SuppressedError" rel="nofollow">MDN constructor page</a> currently links to the old async explicit resource management proposal, which still includes an <code class="notranslate">options</code> parameter and an <code class="notranslate">InstallErrorCause</code> step. The <a href="https://tc39.es/ecma262/multipage/fundamental-objects.html#sec-suppressederror" rel="nofollow">current ECMA-262 constructor</a> takes <code class="notranslate">error</code>, <code class="notranslate">suppressed</code>, and <code class="notranslate">message</code>, matching MDN's documented syntax and note about <code class="notranslate">options</code>.</p>
<p dir="auto"><code class="notranslate">SuppressedError</code> was merged into ECMA-262’s <code class="notranslate">main</code> branch on June 24, 2026, as part of <a href="https://github.com/tc39/ecma262/pull/3000" data-hovercard-type="pull_request" data-hovercard-url="/tc39/ecma262/pull/3000/hovercard">tc39/ecma262#3000</a>, which added Explicit Resource Management. These links should therefore point to the integrated ECMA-262 specification.</p>
<h4 dir="auto">Test results and supporting details</h4>
<ul dir="auto">
<li>Verified that all four replacement links resolve to existing fragment IDs in ECMA-262.</li>
<li><code class="notranslate">npm run prepare</code></li>
<li><code class="notranslate">npm test</code> (passed; ESLint reported 85 warnings and no errors)</li>
<li><code class="notranslate">git diff --check</code></li>
</ul>
<h4 dir="auto">Related issues</h4>
<p dir="auto">None.</p>]]></content>
