        <title type="html"><![CDATA[Add svgView() fragment identifier to SVG <view>]]></title>
        <id>https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/30779</id>
        <link href="https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/30779"/>
        <updated>2026-10-07T13:13:48.000Z</updated>
        <content type="html"><![CDATA[<img src="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/105274?u=173310b843e2751843265438af8cfb79eda02039&v=4" width="64" height="64" alt=""/><br/><h4 dir="auto">Summary</h4>
<ul dir="auto">
<li>Adds the <code class="notranslate">svgView()</code> fragment identifier, as in <code class="notranslate">image.svg#svgView(viewBox(0,0,50,50))</code>, with its <code class="notranslate">viewBox()</code>, <code class="notranslate">preserveAspectRatio()</code> and <code class="notranslate">transform()</code> parameters</li>
<li>Marks <code class="notranslate">transform()</code> as partial in Firefox: it’s applied around the center of the viewport, and after the view box in viewport pixels instead of user units</li>
<li>Versions follow the parent <code class="notranslate">&lt;view&gt;</code> element and its other subfeatures (I think it’s safe to assume they were implemented at the same time)</li>
</ul>
<h4 dir="auto">Test results and supporting details</h4>
<ul dir="auto">
<li>Tested in Chrome 154, Firefox 157 and Safari 27 by drawing <code class="notranslate">&lt;img src="test.svg#svgView(…)"&gt;</code> to a canvas and measuring where known shapes land</li>
<li><code class="notranslate">viewBox()</code>, <code class="notranslate">preserveAspectRatio()</code> and <code class="notranslate">translate()</code> in <code class="notranslate">transform()</code> give the same result in all three</li>
<li><code class="notranslate">transform(scale(0.5))</code> moves a square at 40,40 to 20,20 in Chrome and Safari, and to 45,45 in Firefox</li>
<li>WPT: <a href="https://wpt.fyi/results/svg/linking/reftests/svgview-transform.html" rel="nofollow"><code class="notranslate">svgview-transform.html</code></a> and <a href="https://wpt.fyi/results/svg/linking/reftests/svgview-viewbox-then-transform.html" rel="nofollow"><code class="notranslate">svgview-viewbox-then-transform.html</code></a> fail only in Firefox</li>
<li>Firefox <code class="notranslate">transform()</code> bug: <a href="https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=2066140" rel="nofollow">https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=2066140</a></li>
<li>Firefox 15 implemented <code class="notranslate">&lt;view&gt;</code> and <code class="notranslate">svgView()</code> together: <a href="https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=512525" rel="nofollow">https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=512525</a></li>
<li>Safari ignores the fragment when drawing an image to a canvas that was never inserted into the page, which is a canvas bug rather than an <code class="notranslate">svgView()</code> one: <a href="https://webkit.org/b/322167" rel="nofollow">https://webkit.org/b/322167</a></li>
</ul>
<h4 dir="auto">Related issues</h4>
<ul dir="auto">
<li><a class="issue-link js-issue-link" data-error-text="Failed to load title" data-id="5019644895" data-permission-text="Title is private" data-url="https://github.com/mdn/mdn/issues/852" data-hovercard-type="issue" data-hovercard-url="/mdn/mdn/issues/852/hovercard" href="https://github.com/mdn/mdn/issues/852">mdn/mdn#852</a></li>
</ul>]]></content>
