        <content type="html"><![CDATA[<img src="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/75256866?u=e8b7f1039e5b3d31d8f1d9a206b6046d6c684fc8&v=4" width="64" height="64" alt=""/><br/><p dir="auto"><span class="issue-keyword tooltipped tooltipped-se" aria-label="This pull request closes issue #21132.">Fixes</span> <a class="issue-link js-issue-link" data-error-text="Failed to load title" data-id="1971116477" data-permission-text="Title is private" data-url="https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/21132" data-hovercard-type="issue" data-hovercard-url="/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/21132/hovercard" href="https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/21132">#21132</a></p>
<h3 dir="auto">Description</h3>
<p dir="auto"><code class="notranslate">ScreenOrientation.lock()</code> and <code class="notranslate">unlock()</code> previously mirrored <code class="notranslate">chrome_android</code> for Android WebView. As noted by <a class="user-mention notranslate" data-hovercard-type="user" data-hovercard-url="/users/caugner/hovercard" data-octo-click="hovercard-link-click" data-octo-dimensions="link_type:self" href="https://github.com/caugner">@caugner</a> in <a class="issue-link js-issue-link" data-error-text="Failed to load title" data-id="1971116477" data-permission-text="Title is private" data-url="https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/21132" data-hovercard-type="issue" data-hovercard-url="/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/21132/hovercard" href="https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/21132">#21132</a>, based on <a href="https://issues.chromium.org/issues/40409069" rel="nofollow">https://issues.chromium.org/issues/40409069</a>, <code class="notranslate">lock()</code> always throws in WebView Android, so it is not usable there.</p>
<p dir="auto">This PR sets <code class="notranslate">webview_android.version_added: false</code> for <code class="notranslate">api.ScreenOrientation.lock</code> and <code class="notranslate">api.ScreenOrientation.unlock</code>.</p>]]></content>
